        <Document ID="AC58BF0A-5B02-4894-A652-44126004F905">
            <Title>Research Question 3 (RQ3)</Title>
            <Text>Research Question 3 (RQ3): Is there a connection between rushing yards and player’s birth month? In other words, does the month the player was born in influence the total amount of distance the player ran through their career? To minimize data noise, only retired players will be analyzed for this question.
Hypothesis 3 (H3): The team believes there is a week correlation between rushing yards and birth months for NFL players. There are multiple variables that affect a player’s rushing ability, including the birth location, or high school location elevation. Additionally, a player’s genetic makeup may influence oxygen saturation level (see, for example, Gibbens [2018] article on the Bajau’s people ability to stay underwater for up to 13 minutes without physical harm).
</Text>
        </Document>
        <Document ID="7432931F-6F39-463F-A4B7-A9C9C511BF7C">
            <Title>Measures</Title>
        </Document>
