        <Document ID="A5792672-83F0-43FD-9CED-7DB2CADF120B">
            <Title>Research Question 4 (RQ4)</Title>
            <Text>Research Question 4 (RQ4): Is there a connection between the total amount of television viewers of an NFL game and total points scored?
Hypothesis 4 (H4): According to the Antenna Hypothesis of Consciousness, the brain wave length frequency can pick up various “realities” based on a certain “frequency” the brain can be tuned into, and the brain is able to exchange information among other brains as the waves move through a type of unexplored matter (Worden 2026). Therefore, viewers are able to “will” their team to score, resulting in a “dueling battle” between teams, resulting in a higher score for the teams with the most viewers. The team believes there is no connection between television viewers and sum of the total points scored between two teams, and the Antenna Hypothesis of Consciousness is of questionable scientific value. 
</Text>
        </Document>
